# golden_city.script — the city the golden dump is taken from.
#
# (c) Copyright 2026 Liminal HQ, Scott Morris
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# This file is DATA, not code. `tests/golden_city.rs` replays it against a
# fresh `Simulation` and dumps everything observable to
# `golden_city.expected`. Adding a case means adding lines here — no Rust.
#
# Grammar, one directive per line, `#` starts a comment:
#
#   grid <w> <h>                    the map size. Once, first.
#   seed <n>                        the PRNG seed. Once.
#   tick <n>                        advance the sim by n fixed ticks (1/20 s each).
#   <Tool> <x> <y> [<stratum>]      apply a tool. MUST succeed, or the harness panics.
#   refuse <Tool> <x> <y> [<stratum>]
#                                   apply a tool that MUST be refused. The refusal
#                                   message is recorded in the dump, so the guard text
#                                   is pinned too.
#
# `<Tool>` is the Rust `Tool` enum spelled exactly as it is declared in
# `city_sim_protocol::commands` (case-insensitive here). The harness derives
# the name table from the enum, so a renamed tool fails loudly rather than
# silently mismatching.
#
# `<stratum>` is optional and defaults to `surface` — the active view a
# stratum-scoped tool (`WaterPipe`, `Bulldoze`) acts on. `WaterPipe` refuses
# outright unless it is `underground`; `Bulldoze` clears whichever stratum is
# named. Every other tool ignores it. Case-insensitive, same as `<Tool>`.
#
# The map is 24 wide × 16 tall on purpose — not square, so a transposed x/y
# cannot pass unnoticed.

grid 24 16
seed 20260729

# ===========================================================================
# 1. The ground, before anything is built on it
# ===========================================================================
# A 2×2 lake in the south-west. (1,9) gets bulldozed later and must still be
# a lake afterwards — the bulldozer is not a terraformer.
Water 0 8
Water 1 8
Water 0 9
Water 1 9

# A forest block, so the wilderness patch bonus and the fragmentation penalty
# both have something to say.
Tree 5 10
Tree 6 10
Tree 7 10
Tree 5 11
Tree 6 11
Tree 7 11
Tree 5 12
Tree 6 12

# ===========================================================================
